{"text": " Okay, Caspa just did something Bitcoin has been arguing about for years. It is called a Covenant. A Covenant is a rule that lives inside the coin itself. The coin carries its own rules and enforces them, send only here, locked until later. Royalties, you cannot skip. This is the Tokata hard fork, the biggest upgrade to Caspa since crescendo, and the whole network moves together with no chain split. Ethereum needs a full virtual machine on every node, a giant attack surface. Caspa does not. It teaches the coins the rules directly. Same proof of work security as Bitcoin. With the programmability, Bitcoin still cannot agree on. That unlocks native tokens, Realdify, NFTs, Volts, and Escrow on the fastest base layer in crypto. The story that Caspa is just a fast payments coin is over. Covenants put Caspa light years ahead of every other crypto. This changes what a coin can be.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 4.92, "text": " Okay, Caspa just did something Bitcoin has been arguing about for years.", "tokens": [50364, 1033, 11, 16100, 4306, 445, 630, 746, 11414, 575, 668, 19697, 466, 337, 924, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.25251210410639924, "compression_ratio": 1.5603112840466926, "no_speech_prob": 0.029027683660387993, "words": [{"word": " Okay,", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.34, "probability": 0.44214701652526855}, {"word": " Caspa", "start": 0.7, "end": 1.04, "probability": 0.5863470882177353}, {"word": " just", "start": 1.04, "end": 1.34, "probability": 0.9708006978034973}, {"word": " did", "start": 1.34, "end": 1.66, "probability": 0.9887931942939758}, {"word": " something", "start": 1.66, "end": 2.04, "probability": 0.991973876953125}, {"word": " Bitcoin", "start": 2.04, "end": 2.58, "probability": 0.8769080638885498}, {"word": " has", "start": 2.58, "end": 3.1, "probability": 0.9869588017463684}, {"word": " been", "start": 3.1, "end": 3.34, "probability": 0.9975357055664062}, {"word": " arguing", "start": 3.34, "end"